      "bootstrap_unit": "hearing",
      "multiple_comparisons": "holm, one family per question: E1 (retrievers) compares every retriever with baseline_retriever on the same unit kind, one family per benchmark, split group, unit kind and test (McNemar on acc@1, sign-flip on reciprocal rank); E2 (units) compares every unit kind with baseline_unit for the same retriever on the paired lift (hit@1 minus n_relevant / n_units), one family per benchmark, split group and retriever; no test crosses both the retriever and the unit kind, and every adjusted p-value records its family",
      "multiple_comparisons_amendment": "Recorded on 2026-09-23, before any summarize run that included a dense retriever: the first version tested every (retriever, unit) pair against serafim_335m on sentences with raw acc@1 and MRR in one family per benchmark and split group, which mixed the retriever and unit questions and rewarded larger units for their higher chance of holding a relevant unit (random_acc_at_1 0.015 on B1 sentences vs 0.455 on B1 turns; 1,365 of 3,222 B2 turn queries have every unit relevant); the only summarize report written before this change (retrieval_v1_report.json of the sparse run) had no baseline rows, so no comparison had been computed",
